      "body": "## Motivation\n\nFixes #44748.\n\nA multimodal request carrying a single grayscale JPEG crashes in the HF image processor's normalize step with:\n\n```\nRuntimeError: output with shape [1, 1, 1760, 1248] doesn't match the broadcast shape [1, 3, 1760, 1248]\n```\n\nRoot cause: on the preprocess-cache path, `MediaArtifactCacheMixin.decode_media_snapshot` (`python/sglang/srt/multimodal/media_artifacts/base.py`) decodes the raw source into a PIL image but returns it untouched — a grayscale image stays mode `\"L\"` and reaches the HF processor as 1-channel, which the 3-channel mean/std broadcast rejects. The legacy (non-cache) path never had this problem: `BaseMultimodalProcessor._load_multimodal_inputs` defaults `discard_alpha_channel=True`, converting every non-RGB image via `smart_to_rgb`/`convert(\"RGB\")` before the processor ever sees it.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `python/sglang/srt/multimodal/media_artifacts/base.py`\n  - `decode_media_snapshot` now normalizes every decoded PIL image through a new `_ensure_rgb_image` helper (both the direct-PIL-input branch and the `load_image` branch).\n  - `_ensure_rgb_image` mirrors the legacy path exactly: RGB images are returned as-is (identity, no copy); non-RGB images go through `smart_to_rgb` when the processor class opts into `smart_rgb_conversion` (e.g. GLM-4V), otherwise plain `Image.convert(\"RGB\")`. The attribute is read via `getattr` so the bare mixin (as used in unit tests) keeps working.\n  - Tensor/ndarray paths are untouched, matching the legacy behavior for GPU-decoded tensors.\n  - Conversion happens after decode, so snapshot identity (content digest, artifact key) computed from the raw source is unchanged.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Wrote a stub harness (`/tmp/verify_44748.py`) that executes the **real** `decode_media_snapshot`/`_ensure_rgb_image` from the edited file (torch, `Modality`, cache helpers, and `load_image` stubbed; real PIL/numpy and the real `smart_to_rgb` extracted from `utils/common.py`). 12/12 pass:\n  - Issue repro: grayscale JPEG (`Image.new(\"L\", ...)` saved as JPEG, as in the issue) decodes to mode `\"RGB\"`; an emulated torchvision normalize broadcast with 3-channel mean/std no longer raises; pixel content is preserved across all three channels (all 128).\n  - RGB JPEG passthrough keeps mode `\"RGB\"` with no conversion.\n  - RGBA without `smart_rgb_conversion` converts via plain `convert(\"RGB\")` (same as legacy).\n  - RGBA with `smart_rgb_conversion=True` composites the alpha onto a background (transparent pixel renders white, not the black-drop of plain convert).\n  - Direct PIL `\"L\"` and palette `\"P\"` inputs convert to `\"RGB\"`; ndarray/tensor inputs pass through untouched; non-image modality still raises `NotImplementedError`; malformed image bytes still raise `ValueError` (preserves the contract asserted by `test_media_artifact_processor.py::test_default_image_decoder_rejects_lazy_pil_failure`).\n- Not verifiable here: an end-to-end server run with Qwen3.5-VL requires a GPU and the model weights; the actual HF `Qwen2VLImageProcessor._preprocess` normalize call cannot run on this machine.\n- Pre-push audit (mandatory): `ruff check --select F401,F821,F823,UP037` clean, `ruff format --check` clean, `python3 -m py_compile` clean, `git diff --check` clean, no added line over 88 cols.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39130680305](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39130680305)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39130680310](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39130680310)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39130680324](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39130680324)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
